  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The graph of a quadratic function intersects the x-axis at $(1,0)$ and $(5,0)$ and passes through $(0,-5)$. Find the y-coordinate of its vertex.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let $y=a(x-1)(x-5)$. Substituting $(0,-5)$ gives $5a=-5$, so $a=-1$. The axis of symmetry is $x=3$, and $y=-(3-1)(3-5)=4$. The y-coordinate of the vertex is 4.",
